{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:LiftingAndDescent.DescentInvolution","@type":"LeanModule","name":"LiftingAndDescent.DescentInvolution","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DescentInvolution.tau_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DescentInvolution.tau_idem","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-involution.lean#L41-L49","doc":"τₙ is idempotent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DescentInvolution.tau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DescentInvolution.tau","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-involution.lean#L36-L39","doc":"The involution τ = ℓ ∘ 𝔡. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DescentInvolution.retraction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DescentInvolution.retraction","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-involution.lean#L34-L34","doc":"Retraction: 𝔡 ∘ ℓ = id. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DescentInvolution.descent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DescentInvolution.descent","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-involution.lean#L32-L32","doc":"The descent map 𝔡_{n+1}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DescentInvolution.ascent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DescentInvolution.ascent","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-involution.lean#L30-L30","doc":"The ascent embedding ℓₙ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DescentInvolution.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DescentInvolution.mk","kind":"ctor","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-involution.lean#L28-L28","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DescentInvolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DescentInvolution","kind":"structure","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-involution.lean#L21-L34","doc":"The descent involution τₙ = ℓₙ ∘ 𝔡_{n+1} at level n of the brane tower.\n\nGiven ascent ℓₙ : End(Aₙ) → End(A_{n+1}) and descent 𝔡_{n+1},\nthe composition τₙ is idempotent: τₙ² = τₙ.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:descent-involution}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:descent-involution","label":"def:descent-involution","md":"quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-involution.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}